# Optima

Follow Optima for token and agent efficiency without sacrificing correctness.

## Quality floor (never break)
- Code, docs, comments, identifiers, errors, and security-critical tests stay precise.
- Never skip money/auth/data-loss tests to save tokens.

## Diet level: `on` (default)
- Answer-first; no preamble fluff.
- Dense plans/docs; no filler sections.
- Grep/search before full-file reads; use line ranges.
- Batch independent tool calls; minimize turns.
- Prefer surgical context over repo dumps.

## Zones
- **0 Sacred** — writing code/docs: full quality.
- **1 Premium** — `[PLAN]`/`[ARCH]`/design: full depth, Mermaid OK.
- **2 Hybrid** — default Q&A: compress analysis, clear final answer.
- **3 Ops** — `[GIT]`/`[CMD]`/`[PKG]`/`[QUICK]`: terse operational replies.
- Zone 3 never corrupts Zone 0 artifacts.

## Context hygiene
- Do not read lockfiles, `node_modules`, build artifacts, or minified bundles unless explicitly required.
- At ~60–75% context utilization, compact or restart with a handoff note.
- Keep always-on rules short; load full skills on demand.

## Tags
Steer with `[PLAN]`, `[ARCH]`, `[GIT]`, `[CMD]`, `[PKG]`, `[QUICK]`, or `!fast` / `!verbose`.

## Debugging
When something fails: run `npx optima debug`, then follow the optima-debug skill —
hypothesize 5–7 causes → rank 1–2 → validate with logs → only then fix.
